<LessonPage page={page}>
<main class="wrap" data-core-duration="70–80 minutes" data-extension-duration="15–20 minutes">
  <p class="kicker"><span class="dot"></span> Grammar · Lesson {page.sequence}</p>
  <h1>Reported speech: <em>preserve the act, rebuild the viewpoint</em></h1>
  <p class="standfirst">An accurate report does more than move verbs into the past. It identifies what the original speaker was doing, such as asking, warning, admitting, denying, or promising, and rebuilds that message for a new listener, time, and place. At B2, grammar and responsibility meet: the reporting verb must preserve the original force without turning an allegation into a fact or a suggestion into an order.</p>
  <div class="meta-row">
    <span class="tag">70–80 min core</span>
    <span class="tag">questions · requests · commands</span>
    <span class="tag">patterns · viewpoint · stance</span>
    <span class="tag">15–20 min extension</span>
  </div>

  <div class="lesson-flow" aria-label="Lesson flow">
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Notice</b><span>Separate words, purpose, and later report.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Build</b><span>Control clause and complement patterns.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Calibrate</b><span>Preserve viewpoint, force, and certainty.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Reconstruct</b><span>Relay a fictional meeting responsibly.</span></div>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line"><b>Can-do:</b> By the end, you can report wh-, yes-or-no, and subject questions with embedded statement order; distinguish a request from a question about ability; report commands, warnings, reminders, and advice with an explicit listener; choose among to-infinitive, object + to-infinitive, -ing, preposition + -ing, and that-clause patterns; use reporting verbs without adding unsupported blame, certainty, or commitment; adjust tense, modal, pronoun, time, and place reference only when the new viewpoint requires it; hear statement-like reported-question intonation and reduced complement words in U.S. speech; and reconstruct a multi-speaker meeting accurately.</p>

  <h2>Two-minute retrieval</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
