    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>Name Maya as the listener after <span class="ex">told</span>: The coordinator <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="told Maya that the room was ready" data-hint="Tell takes the listener directly before the content clause." data-fix="The coordinator told Maya that the room was ready." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The inspection ended before the later report: He said the team <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="had finished the inspection" data-hint="Past Perfect marks the completed inspection as earlier than the past reporting point." data-fix="He said the team had finished the inspection." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>Complete the established verb pattern: She suggested <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="checking the schedule again" data-hint="Suggest can take an -ing complement when no listener is placed directly after it." data-fix="She suggested checking the schedule again." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice three layers in every report</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Fictional Riverton cooling-center meeting, June 11</h3>
    <p><b>Maya, chair:</b> <span class="ex">“Can the west branch stay open until 9:00 during heat alerts?”</span></p>
    <p><b>Omar, facilities coordinator:</b> <span class="ex">“I forgot to schedule the evening security staff.”</span></p>
    <p><b>Lena, safety officer:</b> <span class="ex">“Do not extend the hours until two guards are confirmed.”</span></p>
    <p><b>Priya, community liaison:</b> <span class="ex">“Please publish the hours in Spanish and English by Friday.”</span></p>
    <p><b>Nia, director:</b> <span class="ex">“I’ll send the final schedule tomorrow.”</span></p>
    <h3>Jordan’s June 13 briefing</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">Jordan said Maya had asked whether the west branch could stay open until 9:00 during heat alerts. Omar had admitted forgetting to schedule the evening security staff. Lena had warned the team not to extend the hours until two guards were confirmed. Priya had asked the communications team to publish the hours in Spanish and English by Friday. Nia had promised to send the final schedule the next day.</span></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Which report names a question rather than answering it?</li>
      <li>Which reporting verb adds acceptance of responsibility?</li>
      <li>Which verb preserves a safety instruction instead of weakening it into a suggestion?</li>
      <li>Which report identifies the person expected to act?</li>
      <li>Which verb adds a commitment that the original <span class="ex">I’ll</span> supports?</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You separated question form, admitted responsibility, safety force, an explicit listener, and a supported commitment.">
    <h3>Discovery check: words, purpose, and viewpoint</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Reported act discovery choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="asked whether">asked whether</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="admitted forgetting">admitted forgetting</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="warned the team not to">warned the team not to</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="asked the communications team to">asked the communications team to</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="promised to">promised to</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>Maya’s original sentence has yes-or-no question form, so Jordan <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="asked whether" data-hint="Use a question-reporting verb plus whether for two possible answers." data-fix="Jordan said Maya had asked whether the branch could stay open." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the branch could stay open.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>Omar openly accepts that he forgot, so Jordan reports that he had <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="admitted forgetting" data-hint="Admit preserves acceptance of an unwelcome fact and takes -ing here." data-fix="Omar had admitted forgetting to schedule the staff." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> to schedule the staff.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>Lena connects her negative instruction to a safety condition, so she had <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="warned the team not to" data-hint="Warn keeps the risk-based force and takes listener + not to." data-fix="Lena had warned the team not to extend the hours." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> extend the hours.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>Priya makes a polite request to a named group, so she had <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="asked the communications team to" data-hint="Ask plus listener plus to-infinitive reports a request to act." data-fix="Priya had asked the communications team to publish the hours." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> publish the hours.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>Nia’s <span class="ex">I’ll</span> is a clear commitment in this context, so she had <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="promised to" data-hint="Promise reports a supported commitment and takes a to-infinitive." data-fix="Nia had promised to send the final schedule." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> send the schedule.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Get to the root: report the communicative act</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Direct speech presents wording as a quotation. Reported speech presents a reporter’s reconstruction. The reconstruction can preserve the original meaning without repeating every word, but the reporter becomes responsible for the verb used to frame it. <span class="ex">Said</span> is relatively neutral. <span class="ex">Admitted</span> presents the content as something the speaker accepted, <span class="ex">denied</span> presents it as something the speaker rejected, and <span class="ex">promised</span> presents it as a commitment.</p>
  <p>Do not choose a stronger verb merely because it sounds advanced. <span class="ex">She said she would review the file</span> is not automatically <span class="ex">She promised to review it</span>. A promise requires evidence of commitment in the original context. Likewise, <span class="ex">claimed</span> can create distance from an assertion, while <span class="ex">confirmed</span> presents information as established in the reporting situation. Neither verb independently proves whether the underlying content is true.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>original act</th><th>common pattern</th><th>responsible example</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>neutral statement</td><td><span class="ex">say + (that) + clause</span></td><td><span class="ex">Omar said that the inspection was complete.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>information to a listener</td><td><span class="ex">tell + person + (that) + clause</span></td><td><span class="ex">Omar told Maya that the inspection was complete.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>question</td><td><span class="ex">ask + wh-clause / if-whether clause</span></td><td><span class="ex">Maya asked when the branch would open.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>request or directive</td><td><span class="ex">ask/tell + person + (not) to</span></td><td><span class="ex">Priya asked us to publish the hours.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>stance toward an action</td><td><span class="ex">admit/deny/suggest + -ing</span></td><td><span class="ex">Omar admitted forgetting. He denied changing the record.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>commitment or refusal</td><td><span class="ex">promise/agree/refuse + to</span></td><td><span class="ex">Nia promised to send it. Eli refused to guess.</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Embed questions without keeping direct-question machinery</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>A reported question is an embedded clause. Keep a wh-word when the original question has one. Use <span class="ex">if</span> or <span class="ex">whether</span> for a yes-or-no question. Inside the embedded clause, use subject before verb and remove question-mark-only machinery such as inversion and <span class="ex">do, does, did</span>: <span class="ex">“Where did she go?” → He asked where she had gone.</span></p>
  <p>A subject question already has subject-before-verb order: <span class="ex">“Who called?” → She asked who had called.</span> Do not insert <span class="ex">did</span>. Use <span class="ex">whether</span>, not initial <span class="ex">if</span>, in the fixed sequence <span class="ex">whether or not</span>. When the reporting context asks about the best action rather than the truth of a whole proposition, a wh-infinitive can be concise: <span class="ex">He asked what to bring.</span></p>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You used embedded statement order, removed do-support, preserved a subject question, selected whether or not, and distinguished an information request from a request to act.">
    <h3>Reported questions: make the clause fit the new sentence</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Reported question choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="when the branch would open">when the branch would open</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="why the guard had left early">why the guard had left early</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="who had approved the schedule">who had approved the schedule</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="whether or not the west branch was available">whether or not the west branch was available</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="what to bring to the meeting">what to bring to the meeting</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="if I could join online">if I could join online</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="how many guards had been confirmed">how many guards had been confirmed</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>Original: <span class="ex">“When will the branch open?”</span> Later report: Maya asked <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="when the branch would open" data-hint="Keep when, change will to future-in-the-past would, and place the subject before the verb." data-fix="Maya asked when the branch would open." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>Original: <span class="ex">“Why did the guard leave early?”</span> Use the careful earlier-event viewpoint: The director asked <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="why the guard had left early" data-hint="Remove did, place the subject first, and use Past Perfect for the departure before the question." data-fix="The director asked why the guard had left early." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>Original subject question: <span class="ex">“Who approved the schedule?”</span> Later report: She asked <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="who had approved the schedule" data-hint="Who is the subject, so do not insert did or another subject." data-fix="She asked who had approved the schedule." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The chair explicitly presents two alternatives and uses the fixed opening sequence with <span class="ex">or not</span>: She asked <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="whether or not the west branch was available" data-hint="Use whether before the immediate sequence or not." data-fix="She asked whether or not the west branch was available." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>The new volunteer wants a concise list of required items, not an answer about truth: He asked <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="what to bring to the meeting" data-hint="Use wh-word plus to-infinitive when the question concerns the appropriate action for the same understood person." data-fix="He asked what to bring to the meeting." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>Original information question about possibility: <span class="ex">“Can you join online?”</span> I reported the question, not a request: She asked <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="if I could join online" data-hint="Use if plus a clause because she wanted to know whether joining was possible." data-fix="She asked if I could join online." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">7</span><span>Original quantity question: <span class="ex">“How many guards have been confirmed?”</span> Later report: Maya asked <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="how many guards had been confirmed" data-hint="Keep the quantity phrase, use subject-before-verb order, and backshift the perfect passive." data-fix="Maya asked how many guards had been confirmed." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Distinguish questions, requests, commands, and warnings</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>The same surface form can perform different acts. <span class="ex">Can you stay until nine?</span> may ask about ability or availability, or it may politely request that someone stay. The surrounding purpose and expected response determine the report: <span class="ex">She asked if I could stay</span> requests information; <span class="ex">She asked me to stay</span> requests action.</p>
  <p>Commands and requests commonly use <span class="ex">verb + listener + (not) to-infinitive</span>. Choose the reporting verb by force and purpose: <span class="ex">asked</span> for a request, <span class="ex">told</span> for a directive, <span class="ex">instructed</span> for a procedural directive, <span class="ex">reminded</span> for something the listener already needed to remember, and <span class="ex">warned</span> when danger or an unwanted consequence is central. Do not erase the listener when the pattern requires one.</p>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You distinguished information from requested action and preserved request, directive, procedure, reminder, warning, and personalized advice patterns.">
    <h3>Choose the act supported by the complete situation</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Reported directive choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="asked if I could stay until nine">asked if I could stay until nine</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="asked me to stay until nine">asked me to stay until nine</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="told everyone to leave through the west door">told everyone to leave through the west door</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="instructed the guards to record every entry">instructed the guards to record every entry</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="reminded us to post the translated notice">reminded us to post the translated notice</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="warned visitors not to use the closed stairwell">warned visitors not to use the closed stairwell</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="advised the team to confirm the budget first">advised the team to confirm the budget first</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>Maya genuinely wanted to know whether I was available and accepted either yes or no. She <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="asked if I could stay until nine" data-hint="The expected response is information about availability, so use if plus a clause." data-fix="Maya asked if I could stay until nine." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>Maya already knew I was available and politely requested the action. She <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="asked me to stay until nine" data-hint="The expected response is accepting or refusing an action request, so name the listener before to." data-fix="Maya asked me to stay until nine." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>During an evacuation, the supervisor gave a clear directive to the whole group. She <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="told everyone to leave through the west door" data-hint="Use told plus the group plus to-infinitive for a direct instruction." data-fix="She told everyone to leave through the west door." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The security manual required a specific recordkeeping procedure. The manager <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="instructed the guards to record every entry" data-hint="Instructed suits a formal procedural direction and requires the listeners." data-fix="The manager instructed the guards to record every entry." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>The team had already agreed to publish both language versions, and Priya brought the task back to their attention. She <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="reminded us to post the translated notice" data-hint="Remind fits an existing obligation or plan the listener might forget." data-fix="She reminded us to post the translated notice." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>A sign and loose railing made the stairwell unsafe. Staff <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="warned visitors not to use the closed stairwell" data-hint="Use warned because the negative instruction is tied to a documented danger." data-fix="Staff warned visitors not to use the closed stairwell." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">7</span><span>The consultant offered a professional recommendation directly to the project team, who could still decide. She <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="advised the team to confirm the budget first" data-hint="Advise plus listener plus to reports personalized guidance rather than an order." data-fix="She advised the team to confirm the budget first." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Learn stance and complement pattern together</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>A reporting verb and its complement form one lexical pattern. Memorizing only the verb meaning is not enough. English uses several families, and some verbs allow more than one well-formed pattern with a related meaning. In U.S. English, <span class="ex">They recommended that the city add shade</span> commonly uses the base form <span class="ex">add</span> after <span class="ex">that</span>. <span class="ex">They recommended adding shade</span> is also standard. Do not use <span class="ex">recommended the city to add</span> for this meaning.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>pattern family</th><th>high-value verbs</th><th>example</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">verb + to</span></td><td>agree, offer, promise, refuse, threaten</td><td><span class="ex">She offered to call. He refused to speculate.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">verb + person + to</span></td><td>advise, ask, encourage, invite, remind, tell, warn</td><td><span class="ex">She reminded us to publish the notice.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">verb + -ing</span></td><td>admit, deny, suggest, recommend</td><td><span class="ex">He denied changing the figures.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">verb + preposition + -ing</span></td><td>apologize for, insist on, object to</td><td><span class="ex">She apologized for sending the old draft.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">verb + person + preposition + -ing</span></td><td>accuse someone of, congratulate someone on</td><td><span class="ex">The speaker accused the vendor of delaying delivery.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">verb + that-clause</span></td><td>acknowledge, claim, complain, confirm, explain, insist</td><td><span class="ex">The record confirms that the inspection occurred.</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You matched eight communicative acts to their complement patterns without adding unsupported certainty, blame, or commitment.">
    <h3>Stance map: preserve what the original speaker actually did</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Omar admitted forgetting to schedule the evening staff." data-hint="His original wording explicitly accepts the omission; use admit plus -ing." data-fix="Omar admitted forgetting to schedule the evening staff."><p class="quiz-question">1. Omar said, “I did forget to schedule the evening staff.” Which report preserves his acceptance?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Omar admitted forgetting to schedule the evening staff.">Omar admitted forgetting to schedule the evening staff.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Omar promised to forget the evening staff.">Omar promised to forget the evening staff.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Omar warned the staff forgetting the schedule.">Omar warned the staff forgetting the schedule.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Omar denied changing the inspection date." data-hint="He rejects the accusation; deny takes an -ing complement." data-fix="Omar denied changing the inspection date."><p class="quiz-question">2. Omar said, “I did not change the inspection date.” Which report preserves his rejection of that accusation without deciding whether he was truthful?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Omar denied changing the inspection date.">Omar denied changing the inspection date.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Omar confirmed changing the inspection date.">Omar confirmed changing the inspection date.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Omar denied to change the inspection date.">Omar denied to change the inspection date.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Nia promised to send the final schedule by noon." data-hint="Her words explicitly make a commitment; promise takes a to-infinitive." data-fix="Nia promised to send the final schedule by noon."><p class="quiz-question">3. Nia said, “You have my word. I will send the final schedule by noon.” Which report preserves the commitment?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Nia promised to send the final schedule by noon.">Nia promised to send the final schedule by noon.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Nia suggested sending the schedule, but made no commitment.">Nia suggested sending the schedule, but made no commitment.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Nia promised that the team sent it yesterday.">Nia promised that the team sent it yesterday.</button></div></div>
