  <h2>Sound natural: make the report sound like a report</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>A direct wh-question often has question intonation, but the embedded question usually sits inside a larger statement and ends with statement-like falling intonation: <span class="ex">She asked where the <strong>FILE was</strong>.</span> A reported yes-or-no question also normally follows the intonation of the whole reporting statement rather than recreating the original question: <span class="ex">He asked whether the branch was <strong>OPEN</strong>.</span></p>
  <p>In ordinary U.S. speech, <span class="ex">that</span> is often omitted after <span class="ex">said</span> and <span class="ex">told</span> when the clause remains clear. The <span class="ex">to</span> in <span class="ex">asked us to WAIT</span> is usually weak /tə/. Stress can correct the reported act: <span class="ex">She <strong>ASKED</strong> me to stay</span> contrasts a polite request with <span class="ex">She <strong>TOLD</strong> me to stay</span>, a directive. Do not claim that one reporting verb always carries stress; stress follows the information contrast.</p>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-lesson-extension="Tutor-read statement-like reported-question intonation, weak that and to, reporting-verb contrast, and contracted viewpoint listening check" data-success-message="Correct. You heard statement-like embedding, a weak to-infinitive, request-versus-directive stress, omitted that, and contracted future-in-the-past.">
    <h3>Listen before opening the transcript</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Ask your tutor to read the five lines naturally. Choose the intended form or meaning, then open the transcript only after checking.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Spoken reported speech choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="where the file was">where the file was</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="asked us to wait">asked us to wait</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="a polite request rather than a directive">a polite request rather than a directive</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="said the branch was ready">said the branch was ready</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="she would call the next day">she would call the next day</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span><span class="contraction">Tutor line 1:</span> <span class="ex">She asked where the file was.</span> Recover the embedded clause with statement order: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="where the file was" data-hint="Listen for the subject file before was and the fall at the end of the whole statement." data-fix="The embedded clause is where the file was." data-placeholder="listen">listen</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span><span class="contraction">Tutor line 2:</span> <span class="ex">They asked us to wait.</span> Recover the complete request despite weak <span class="ex">to</span>: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="asked us to wait" data-hint="Listen for the listener us before weak /tə/ and stressed wait." data-fix="The complete request is asked us to wait." data-placeholder="listen">listen</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span><span class="contraction">Tutor line 3:</span> <span class="ex">She ASKED me to stay; she didn’t TELL me to.</span> The contrast identifies <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="a polite request rather than a directive" data-hint="The speaker corrects the force by contrasting asked with told." data-fix="The line presents a polite request rather than a directive." data-placeholder="listen">listen</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span><span class="contraction">Tutor line 4:</span> <span class="ex">Omar said the branch was ready.</span> No audible <span class="ex">that</span> is required; the full report is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="said the branch was ready" data-hint="Said can be followed directly by the content clause in natural conversation." data-fix="Omar said the branch was ready." data-placeholder="listen">listen</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span><span class="contraction">Tutor line 5:</span> <span class="ex">She said she’d call the next day.</span> The base verb <span class="ex">call</span> shows that <span class="ex">’d</span> means <span class="ex">would</span>, so the meaning is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="she would call the next day" data-hint="Before a base verb, contracted ’d represents would, not had." data-fix="She said she would call the next day." data-placeholder="listen">listen</button>.</span></div>
