  <h2>Build the report from meaning outward</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="maya asked whether the west branch could stay open until nine" data-hint="Begin with the questioner and asked, add whether, then use statement order inside the embedded clause." data-fix="Maya asked whether the west branch could stay open until nine." data-success-message="Correct. Whether introduces the yes-or-no issue, and the embedded clause keeps subject-before-modal statement order.">
    <h3>Builder 1: reported yes-or-no question</h3><p class="tile-target">Build Maya’s question report.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank><button class="tile" data-build-tile="until nine">until nine</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="asked">asked</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="the west branch">the west branch</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="Maya">Maya</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="stay open">stay open</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="could">could</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="whether">whether</button></div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap chunks in order"></div><div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>
  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="lena warned the team not to extend the hours" data-hint="Keep the risk verb first, name the listener, and place not before the to-infinitive." data-fix="Lena warned the team not to extend the hours." data-success-message="Correct. Warned preserves the safety force, while team + not to identifies the listener and negative action.">
    <h3>Builder 2: negative warning</h3><p class="tile-target">Build Lena’s safety report.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank><button class="tile" data-build-tile="the hours">the hours</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="the team">the team</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="warned">warned</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="extend">extend</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="Lena">Lena</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="to">to</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="not">not</button></div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap chunks in order"></div><div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>
  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="omar denied changing the inspection date but admitted forgetting the staff" data-hint="Use deny and admit with -ing, and preserve the contrast between the rejected allegation and accepted omission." data-fix="Omar denied changing the inspection date but admitted forgetting the staff." data-success-message="Correct. The two -ing patterns preserve opposite stances toward two different actions.">
    <h3>Builder 3: contrast denial and admission</h3><p class="tile-target">Build Omar’s two-part stance report.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank><button class="tile" data-build-tile="the inspection date">the inspection date</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="but admitted">but admitted</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="Omar">Omar</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="forgetting">forgetting</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="changing">changing</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="the staff">the staff</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="denied">denied</button></div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap chunks in order"></div><div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice and repair the distorted report</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="did the branch close" data-hint="A reported wh-question needs subject-before-verb order and no do-support." data-fix="Maya asked why the branch had closed early." data-why="The question is embedded inside a statement, and the closure occurred before Maya’s past question." data-success-message="Correct. The repair removes do-support, restores statement order, and marks the earlier closure clearly.">
    <h3>Repair 1: embedded question order</h3><p>Tap the phrase that keeps direct-question machinery.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="maya">Maya asked</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="why">why</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="did the branch close">did the branch close</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="early">early.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="suggested us to add" data-hint="Suggest does not take listener + to-infinitive in this meaning." data-fix="The panel suggested adding text alerts. Alternatively: The panel suggested that the city add text alerts." data-why="Use suggest + -ing or, in standard U.S. English, suggest + that + subject + base verb." data-success-message="Correct. The repair selects a standard suggest pattern instead of borrowing the ask-or-advise pattern.">
    <h3>Repair 2: complement after <span class="ex">suggest</span></h3><p>Tap the phrase with the borrowed complement pattern.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="panel">The panel</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="suggested us to add">suggested us to add</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="alerts">text alerts</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="meeting">at the meeting.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="warned not to enter" data-hint="Warn normally needs the person who receives the warning before not to." data-fix="The safety officer warned visitors not to enter the stairwell." data-why="The object visitors identifies who must avoid the unsafe action." data-success-message="Correct. The repair restores the listener required by this warning pattern.">
    <h3>Repair 3: restore the listener</h3><p>Tap the phrase that leaves the warning recipient missing.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="officer">The safety officer</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="warned not to enter">warned not to enter</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="stairwell">the stairwell</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="inspection">during the inspection.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="promised" data-hint="The original speaker only predicted what was likely; no commitment is documented." data-fix="The analyst said the temperature would probably fall after sunset. Alternatively: The analyst predicted that it would probably fall." data-why="Promised adds personal commitment that the original prediction does not contain." data-success-message="Correct. The repair removes an unsupported commitment and preserves the original prediction.">
    <h3>Repair 4: remove added stance</h3><p>The analyst said, <span class="ex">“The temperature will probably fall after sunset.”</span> Tap the reporting verb that distorts this prediction.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="analyst">The analyst</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="promised">promised</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="temperature">that the temperature would probably fall</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="sunset">after sunset.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Say the report before you reveal it</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-transform>
    <h3>Guided oral reconstruction</h3>
    <p>Read the exact context, make one complete report aloud, and reveal only after you answer.</p>
    <div class="transform-list">
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>1</b> Direct wh-question: <span class="ex">“Why did the west door close?”</span> Use a careful later viewpoint.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>She asked why the west door had closed.</strong></p></div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>2</b> Polite action request: <span class="ex">“Please send me the signed schedule.”</span> The speaker addressed Jordan.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>She asked Jordan to send her the signed schedule.</strong></p></div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>3</b> Negative safety instruction: <span class="ex">“Do not use the west stairwell.”</span> Staff addressed visitors.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>Staff warned visitors not to use the west stairwell.</strong></p></div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>4</b> Accepted action and rejected allegation: <span class="ex">“I forgot the staff schedule, but I did not change the inspection date.”</span></p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>He admitted forgetting the staff schedule but denied changing the inspection date.</strong></p></div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>5</b> U.S. that-clause recommendation: <span class="ex">“The city should add text alerts.”</span> Use <span class="ex">recommended</span>.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>The panel recommended that the city add text alerts.</strong></p></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Practice reporting without exposing private information</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>You never need to report a real disciplinary meeting, accusation, legal conversation, medical discussion, financial dispute, immigration interview, confidential workplace event, family conflict, or identifiable person. Use Riverton, public statements with a reliable source, or a tutor-created fictional meeting. The goal is accurate reconstruction, not disclosure.</p>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Question shift:</b> Draw a fictional direct question. Report it once as an information question and, if the wording permits, once as an action request. Explain what contextual change makes the second reading possible.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Force ladder:</b> Report three fictional instructions with <span class="ex">asked, told</span>, and <span class="ex">warned</span>. Give the relationship, risk, and expected response that justify each verb.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Pattern audit:</b> Choose five reporting verbs from different complement families. Say the full pattern before adding content: <span class="ex">deny doing, promise to do, remind someone to do, apologize for doing, confirm that...</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Viewpoint challenge:</b> Move one message from the same room and day to a different place three days later. Change only the pronouns, tenses, modals, and reference words whose meaning requires a new form.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Stance editor:</b> Replace an overstrong reporting verb with a neutral one, or replace a vague <span class="ex">said</span> with a more precise verb when the original context supports it. Defend the change.</div>

  <h2>Final production and check</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Final production: give a 90-second meeting reconstruction</h3>
    <p>Use Riverton or another tutor-supplied fictional record. Establish the original date, place, speakers, and listeners, then report at least seven contributions. Include one wh-question, one yes-or-no question, one polite request, one negative warning or command, one admission or denial, one proposal, and one supported commitment. Use at least four complement families. Adjust one calendar reference and one person reference. Preserve one current fact without backshift only if you explicitly verify that it is still current. Separate what the source says from what later evidence confirms. When your listener challenges one reporting verb, reformulate the sentence more neutrally or defend the stronger verb from the original wording.</p>
    <p><b>Success criteria:</b> Can the listener recover who originally spoke to whom, the original communicative act, the requested or reported content, the relevant time and place, the reporting verb’s complement pattern, the speaker’s degree of commitment or responsibility, and the boundary between quoted evidence and the reporter’s interpretation?</p>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You preserved embedded order, request force, reporting-verb pattern, verified viewpoint, source boundaries, and natural spoken contrast.">
    <h3>Final check: form, meaning, use, and responsibility</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="She asked why the west door had closed early." data-hint="Use embedded statement order with no do-support, and mark the closure before the past question." data-fix="She asked why the west door had closed early."><p class="quiz-question">1. Which sentence accurately reports <span class="ex">“Why did the west door close early?”</span> from a later viewpoint?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="She asked why the west door had closed early.">She asked why the west door had closed early.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="She asked why did the west door close early?">She asked why did the west door close early?</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="She asked why had closed the west door early.">She asked why had closed the west door early.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="She asked me to stay until nine because another staff member had called out." data-hint="The context says she wanted the action, so use listener + to-infinitive." data-fix="She asked me to stay until nine because another staff member had called out."><p class="quiz-question">2. The coordinator knew I was available and politely requested that I remain. Which report preserves the action request?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="She asked me to stay until nine because another staff member had called out.">She asked me to stay until nine because another staff member had called out.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="She asked if I could stay until nine only because she wanted information and no action.">She asked if I could stay until nine only because she wanted information and no action.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="She suggested me to staying until nine.">She suggested me to staying until nine.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The panel recommended that the city add text alerts." data-hint="Use recommend plus that-clause and the U.S. base form add." data-fix="The panel recommended that the city add text alerts."><p class="quiz-question">3. Which U.S. English sentence has the intended recommendation pattern?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The panel recommended that the city add text alerts.">The panel recommended that the city add text alerts.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The panel recommended that the city added text alerts yesterday, although the action is only proposed.">The panel recommended that the city added text alerts yesterday, although the action is only proposed.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The panel recommended the city to add text alerts.">The panel recommended the city to add text alerts.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The June 7 certificate says the cooling system is safe, and today’s inspection log confirms that the certificate is still current." data-hint="The current source and today’s verification support a present viewpoint." data-fix="The June 7 certificate says the system is safe, and today’s log confirms the information is still current."><p class="quiz-question">4. Which report justifies retaining a present form rather than backshifting mechanically?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The June 7 certificate says the cooling system is safe, and today’s inspection log confirms that the certificate is still current.">The June 7 certificate says the cooling system is safe, and today’s inspection log confirms that the certificate is still current.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The system was safe once, so it must remain safe forever without another check.">The system was safe once, so it must remain safe forever without another check.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Every verb after any reporting expression must move one tense back regardless of time or meaning.">Every verb after any reporting expression must move one tense back regardless of time or meaning.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The speaker accused the vendor of delaying delivery; the available record does not yet establish that accusation as fact." data-hint="Keep the accusation attributed to its speaker and state the evidence limit." data-fix="The speaker accused the vendor of delaying delivery; the record does not yet establish the accusation as fact."><p class="quiz-question">5. Which sentence preserves a strong allegation without endorsing it?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The speaker accused the vendor of delaying delivery; the available record does not yet establish that accusation as fact.">The speaker accused the vendor of delaying delivery; the available record does not yet establish that accusation as fact.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The vendor certainly delayed delivery and caused every later problem, although the evidence is incomplete.">The vendor certainly delayed delivery and caused every later problem, although the evidence is incomplete.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The speaker accused that the vendor delayed to deliver.">The speaker accused that the vendor delayed to deliver.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Stress ASKED to correct the force, and keep to weak in asked me to stay." data-hint="Contrastive stress belongs on the corrected reporting verb; unstressed to is normally reduced." data-fix="She ASKED me to stay; she didn’t TELL me to. Keep to weak unless it is itself contrasted."><p class="quiz-question">6. You are correcting someone who described a polite request as an order. Which spoken choice is natural?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Stress ASKED to correct the force, and keep to weak in asked me to stay.">Stress ASKED to correct the force, and keep to weak in asked me to stay.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Stress every word equally because reported speech has no information focus.">Stress every word equally because reported speech has no information focus.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Use direct-question rising intonation after every reported question and every command.">Use direct-question rising intonation after every reported question and every command.</button></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button></div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Reflect: can you defend the reporting verb?</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Explain the reconstruction path</h3>
    <p>Complete these ideas aloud: <span class="ex">The original speaker was...</span> <span class="ex">The original listener was...</span> <span class="ex">The speaker was asking / requesting / directing / warning / admitting / denying / proposing / committing because...</span> <span class="ex">This reporting verb takes...</span> <span class="ex">The original reference point was...</span> <span class="ex">The new reference point is...</span> <span class="ex">I changed / retained the tense because...</span> <span class="ex">The source supports...</span> <span class="ex">The source does not establish...</span></p>
    <p>Then choose one sentence from your reconstruction. Replace its reporting verb with <span class="ex">said</span>. Explain what useful meaning disappears. Put the precise verb back only if the original wording and situation support it.</p>
    <p><a href="#next-day-retrieval">Return tomorrow for the five-item retrieval check</a> before rereading the lesson.</p>
  </div>

  <section id="next-day-retrieval" data-lesson-extension="Next-day embedded-question, directive-force, complement-pattern, viewpoint, and stance-calibration retrieval">
    <h2>Next-day retrieval</h2>
    <div class="lead-rule"></div>
    <p>Return without rereading the page. Recover the embedded order, reporting act, complement family, time viewpoint, and evidence boundary from new fictional contexts.</p>
    <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You retained embedded statement order, warning force, an -ing complement, calendar-aware viewpoint, and responsible allegation framing.">
      <h3>Five delayed checks</h3>
      <div class="quiz-list">
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The coordinator asked when the replacement bus would arrive." data-hint="Keep when, place the subject before would, and remove direct-question order." data-fix="The coordinator asked when the replacement bus would arrive."><p class="quiz-question">1. Which sentence accurately reports <span class="ex">“When will the replacement bus arrive?”</span>?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The coordinator asked when the replacement bus would arrive.">The coordinator asked when the replacement bus would arrive.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The coordinator asked when would the replacement bus arrive?">The coordinator asked when would the replacement bus arrive?</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The coordinator asked when did the replacement bus would arrive.">The coordinator asked when did the replacement bus would arrive.</button></div></div>
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The guide warned visitors not to cross the barrier because the floor was unstable." data-hint="The danger justifies warned, and the negative pattern needs the listeners before not to." data-fix="The guide warned visitors not to cross the barrier because the floor was unstable."><p class="quiz-question">2. Which report preserves a risk-based negative instruction?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The guide warned visitors not to cross the barrier because the floor was unstable.">The guide warned visitors not to cross the barrier because the floor was unstable.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The guide suggested visitors to cross the unstable floor.">The guide suggested visitors to cross the unstable floor.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The guide warned not visitors crossing the barrier.">The guide warned not visitors crossing the barrier.</button></div></div>
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The editor denied removing the source note." data-hint="Deny takes an -ing complement for the rejected action." data-fix="The editor denied removing the source note."><p class="quiz-question">3. The editor said, <span class="ex">“I did not remove the source note.”</span> Which report has the correct stance and pattern?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The editor denied removing the source note.">The editor denied removing the source note.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The editor denied to remove the source note.">The editor denied to remove the source note.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The editor promised removing the source note.">The editor promised removing the source note.</button></div></div>
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="On Friday, Luis said he had sent the form the previous day, which meant Thursday." data-hint="Use Past Perfect and resolve the original yesterday from the known Friday speaking date." data-fix="On Friday, Luis said he had sent the form the previous day, which meant Thursday."><p class="quiz-question">4. Luis spoke on Friday: <span class="ex">“I sent the form yesterday.”</span> Which later report keeps the calendar relationship clear?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="On Friday, Luis said he had sent the form the previous day, which meant Thursday.">On Friday, Luis said he had sent the form the previous day, which meant Thursday.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="On Friday, Luis said he sends the form tomorrow, which meant Monday.">On Friday, Luis said he sends the form tomorrow, which meant Monday.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Luis said yesterday forever refers to the reporter’s current day.">Luis said yesterday forever refers to the reporter’s current day.</button></div></div>
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The resident accused the contractor of blocking the entrance; the inspection has not yet established who caused the obstruction." data-hint="Attribute the accusation and keep the unresolved evidence boundary explicit." data-fix="The resident accused the contractor of blocking the entrance; the inspection has not yet established who caused it."><p class="quiz-question">5. Which report preserves an unresolved accusation responsibly?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The resident accused the contractor of blocking the entrance; the inspection has not yet established who caused the obstruction.">The resident accused the contractor of blocking the entrance; the inspection has not yet established who caused the obstruction.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The contractor certainly blocked the entrance because an accusation is proof.">The contractor certainly blocked the entrance because an accusation is proof.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The resident accused that the contractor to block the entrance.">The resident accused that the contractor to block the entrance.</button></div></div>
      </div>
